Applications received after the start of review may be considered if an acceptable candidate is not identified. Specific questions related to this search should be directed to Dr. Janet Wojcik at wojcikj@winthrop.edu.

Job Description
SCHOOL OF CHINESE MEDICINE
CENTRE FOR CHINESE HERBAL MEDICINE DRUG DEVELOPMENT
Research Assistant Professor (26270203)
The School of Chinese Medicine (SCM) at Hong Kong Baptist University is seeking a high calibre Research Assistant Professor to join in the Centre for Chinese Herbal Medicine Drug Development (CDD), which is located in the Hong Kong Science Park.
Responsibilities:
Design, lead, and publish hypothesis-driven clinical research on the new drug development;
Develop and submit grant proposals to secure extramural funding for clinical and translational research;
Serve as Principal Investigator (PI) or Sub-Investigator on multiple interventional trials, designing phase-appropriate trial protocols, overseeing patient recruitment, informed consent, protocol adherence, and data integrity, leading safety monitoring and DSMB reporting;
Integrate translational endpoints into trial designs to support go/no-go decisions and registration strategies;
Contribute to regulatory submissions (IND/CTA applications, NDA/BLA supporting documentation);
Supervise junior researchers and students; and
Undertake any other duties as assigned.
Requirements:
Hold a Ph.D. degree in a relevant biomedical field (e.g., Chinese medicine, pharmacology, immunology, or epidemiology., etc) from an accredited institution, with postdoctoral research experience preferred;
At least 3 years of hands-on experience in conducting clinical trials as a study leader or senior clinical scientist, especially with experience on Chinese medicine-related clinical studies;
Demonstrated capacity to independently design research protocols, interpret scientific findings, and maintain a strong publication record, and an established track record in obtaining external funding/research grants;
Innovative, self-motivated with good planning and organisational skills;
Team-oriented, with excellent communication skills; and
Good English communication skills and the ability to write clearly.
Work Location: Hong Kong Science Park and Hong Kong Baptist University
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract for up to three years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to mutual agreement.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System with samples of publications, preferably three best ones out of their most recent publications/works, a brief statement of their research interest and research plan. Those who are not invited for interview 4 months after the closing date may consider their applications unsuccessful. All application materials including publication samples, scholarly/creative works will be disposed of after completion of the recruitment exercise. Details of the University s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacypolicy.
The University reserves the right not to make appointments for the posts advertised, and the appointments will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

Job Description
SCHOOL OF CHINESE MEDICINE
TEACHING AND RESEARCH DIVISION
Research Assistant Professor (26270218)
The School of Chinese Medicine (SCM) at Hong Kong Baptist University is seeking a high-calibre Research Assistant Professor to join the Hong Kong Calculus Bovis Research Centre (CBRC). We are particularly interested in a candidate who can bridge the gap between traditional Chinese medicine (TCM) and modern immunology to spearhead the scientific modernisation of TCM.
Responsibilities:
Conduct high-quality and innovative research to elucidate the immunological and pharmacological mechanisms of Calculus Bovis and related natural components, applying cutting-edge techniques from mucosal immunology and innate immune signalling;
Lead and participate in multiple interdisciplinary R&D projects to drive the translational development of TCM-based drug candidates, leveraging your expertise in modulating immune responses for therapeutic benefit;
Transfer academic knowledge into innovative technologies for impactful research outputs, for instance, by exploring TCM components as novel immune adjuvants or modulators;
Supervise junior researchers and students in projects that integrate natural product chemistry with advanced immunological assays; and
Undertake any other duties as assigned to advance the Centre's research goals.
Requirements:
Hold a Ph.D. degree in Immunology, Pharmacology, Medicinal Chemistry, Natural Product Chemistry, or related disciplines, with significant postdoctoral research experience;
Demonstrated expertise in elucidating the mechanisms of natural products, particularly in how they modulate mucosal immunity and systemic immune responses;
Demonstrated capacity to design research protocols independently, interpret scientific findings, and maintain a strong publication record;
Innovative, self-motivated with good planning and organisational skills;
Team-oriented, with excellent communication skills; and
Good English communication skills and the ability to write clearly.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks/4 months after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University's Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.
